  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Livelihood Enhancement LEP) for poor farmers of Chiakariga sub-County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Livelihood Enhancement Project aims to empower 150 rural farmers [90 women and 60 men] in five locations in Chiakariga Sub-County through hands-on training in sustainable agriculture and goat husbandry. By enhancing food security, increasing income, and promoting self-reliance, the project seeks to improve the livelihoods of these farmers. Additionally, it facilitates the establishment of Self-help savings and credit group (SHGs) to ensure long-term sustainability. By actively engaging with stakeholders at all levels, the project addresses cultural and patriarchal barriers hindering community development, specifically targeting women&apos;s socio-economic transformation.</narrative>
  </description>
